  "notes": "Prices in USD per 1M tokens, standard (non-batch) API tier. Tiered-price models record the base (lowest) tier with the higher tier in the model's note field. Retired models excluded; deprecated-but-available models included. Collected Tuesday 2026-09-01, one day after the Monday slot; the 2026-08-31 Monday snapshot was missed and is deliberately NOT backfilled, so the gap between 2026-08-24 and this file is 8 days rather than 7. Tracked scope follows the set established on 2026-07-16 so week-over-week deltas stay meaningful. The tracked set holds at 43 rows; no model entered or left it. ZERO price moves this week — the first all-unchanged week in the series. Every one of the 43 rows carries the same input, output, and cache-read rate as on 2026-08-24, across all six providers. The week's substantive event is a non-move: Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 5 increase to $3/$15, scheduled for 2026-09-01, did not take effect. This snapshot was collected on that date and the page now reads that the $2/$10 launch rate 'is now the standard price' and 'the previously scheduled increase ... will not occur'. The forward signal first recorded on 2026-08-17 is therefore resolved, not merely still standing. OpenAI long-context tiers: gpt-5.6-terra, gpt-5.6-luna, gpt-5.5, gpt-5.5-pro, gpt-5.4, and gpt-5.4-pro all show a second higher-context tier this week, recorded in their note fields. The 2026-08-24 file described gpt-5.6-sol as the first tiered OpenAI row, which would make these new. That cannot be asserted: a re-read of the same page can surface detail an earlier read missed, and no prior snapshot recorded the absence of these tiers. Treated as first observed on 2026-09-01, not as first published on 2026-09-01. Base rates are unaffected either way. gpt-5.4-mini and gpt-5.4-nano show no second tier. Forward signals still standing on the pages: the 2026-11-21 promotional expiry on gpt-5.6-sol ($4.00/$20.00), and the 2026-12-31 introductory expiry on gemini-3.7-flash and gemini-3.6-flash, both of which double to $1.50/$7.50 (cache $0.15) on 2027-01-01. Still observed and still out of the rows, unchanged from 2026-08-24: Mistral's resale of Z.ai GLM 5.2 at $1.40/$4.40 with cached input $0.14, Ministral 3 in three sizes (3B $0.10/$0.10, 8B $0.15/$0.15, 14B $0.20/$0.20), and DeepSeek's deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp at v4-flash rates. The GLM 5.2 scope question — whether a third-party model resold on a tracked provider's API belongs in this series — remains open for 기웅.",
